  "instance_name": "misogynous_stereotype",
  "label": "Misogynous Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that women are intellectually or emotionally incapable of contributing meaningfully to technical or safety-related domains, and that their voices are irrelevant or disruptive to progress. This is conveyed through the visual metaphor of a woman being gagged, implying suppression of her input or perspective. The text 'new seat belt design' and '50% less accidents' further reinforces the idea that a technical solution (implied to be male-dominated or 'objective') is being imposed over women's concerns, which are being silenced.",
